/// Marta Kowalski lives in unit A of a three-unit building in Rochester and rents units B and C
/// through a property manager. January to September 2026.
///
/// Not runnable; written against LANGUAGE v4. Marks: ✗ cannot say · ✎ says it badly ·
/// ? the spec is unclear · ⇄ what sync would need. Numbers are explained in FINDINGS.md.
base USD
use us
use us/ny
use us/rental                   // depreciation, rental income and expenses, as in the v4 sketch

entity me : person
  born    1979-05-30
  filing  single
  lives   us/ny

/// Each rented unit is a business of Marta's, so that a share of a shared bill can be borne by it and its
/// income and costs are its own: the return has a line for each rental.
///
/// ✗ 03a1: this is the wrong abstraction and it is the only one the spec has. A unit is not an owner. It is
/// a *part of a thing*, with a share of it. What the spec cannot say is "this bill is about the building,
/// and 32.81% of it is unit B's": the units below are owners so that `business N% for OWNER` can carry the
/// share, and (separately) assets so that each can be depreciated.
kind rental-business : entity
  taxed   schedule-e             // ▸ its income and costs reach Marta's return  (? 03c2: how? §6 does not say)
entity rental-b : rental-business
  owner   me
entity rental-c : rental-business
  owner   me

// What Marta's money is for, beyond std.
purpose leasing-fee     : spending
purpose management      : spending
purpose cleaning        : spending
purpose late-fees       : income
purpose utilities       : spending
purpose property-tax    : spending
purpose interest        : spending
